# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The policy is deliberately permissive about INLINE code and strict about ORIGINS, because that
# split matches where the risk actually is here:
#
#   · The application uses plain same-origin scripts and styles, a small inline theme bootstrap,
#     inline event handlers and style attributes. Cloudflare injects its own bot-detection
#     script whose inline body embeds a per-request ray id — its hash changes every request, so no
#     static hash list can ever cover it, and a strict script-src would break bot detection on the
#     custom domain. 'unsafe-inline' is the honest choice rather than a policy that silently fails.
#
#   · What IS worth locking down is where data can go. This page pulls from a fixed set of public
#     NOAA / Open-Meteo endpoints (plus the Iowa Environmental Mesonet's storm reports, fetched only
#     during the storm layout) and talks to nothing else. connect-src below is the real control:
#     it means a future bug (or a compromised CDN dependency) cannot exfiltrate to an arbitrary host.
#
# Keep in sync with the origins the app actually uses — every entry was taken from an audit of the
# source, not guessed. Adding a new feed means adding it here or the fetch fails.
#
# www.weather.gov is likewise in both: the Weather Story's XML (titles, captions, valid times) is a
# fetch, and its graphics are images.
#
# gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov appears in BOTH img-src and connect-src, which looks like a duplicate and
# isn't: the satellite TILES are images, and the list of which timestamps exist is a fetch. GIBS
# publishes GeoColor on a ~10-minute cadence with real gaps in it — a missing slot is a hard 404 —
# so scrubbing the radar back has to ask DescribeDomains which moments actually exist rather than
# compute them. Two directives because they are genuinely two kinds of access to one host.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://www.weather.gov https://gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov https://opengeo.ncep.noaa.gov https://tiles.openfreemap.org https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://api.weather.gov https://api.water.noaa.gov https://mapservices.weather.noaa.gov https://services5.arcgis.com https://data.rcc-acis.org https://opengeo.ncep.noaa.gov https://gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov https://tiles.openfreemap.org https://api.open-meteo.com https://air-quality-api.open-meteo.com https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu https://www.weather.gov; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Mutable asset paths must revalidate. Versioned URLs also bypass copies already fresh in browsers.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Generated NBM data is mutable; enable serving only after the publication review.
/data/nbm-range.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/data/nbm-hourly.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# UpperAir sounding viewer, built from the private skew-t-viewer repo by its
# scripts/sync_lsxdashboard.sh and committed here as finished files (SOURCE_COMMIT says which).
# It is a separate app with a separate, smaller origin list, so it detaches the dashboard's CSP
# rather than widening it: `!` removes the header the `/*` rule set, and the line after sets its
# own. Without the detach both policies would apply and the stricter intersection would block
# USGS basemap tiles. blob: is for the PNG export preview, which the dashboard never needs.
# tools/check.py verifies every origin in the bundle is covered here.
/upperair/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://api.open-meteo.com https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu https://basemap.nationalmap.gov; worker-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; manifest-src 'self'

# Vite names these files by content hash, so a changed file is a new URL and old ones never change.
/upperair/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/upperair/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/upperair/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate
